{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.OrbitalSpaceNormalBundle","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.OrbitalSpaceNormalBundle","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Finrank","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalSpaceNormalBundle.ConditionalAudit.orbital_space_normal_bundle_conditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalSpaceNormalBundle.ConditionalAudit.orbital_space_normal_bundle_conditional","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L213-L225","doc":"**Orbital-space dimension law (conditional on `BorromeanQuark`).**\nGiven the Borromean-quark SO(3) decomposition `O_n ≅ ⊕_{ℓ<n} V_ℓ`, the\norbital space at shell `n` has dimension `n²`:\n\n  `dim O_n = n²`.\n\nDerived from the class field `so3_decomposition` (the conjectural\ninput) and the unconditional arithmetic identity `orbital_space_dim`\nproved above — a genuine equation, not `True`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalSpaceNormalBundle.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.so3_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalSpaceNormalBundle.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.so3_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L210-L210","doc":"**Conjectural input.** The orbital dimension at shell `n` is the sum\nof the SO(3)-irrep dimensions `2ℓ+1` of the admitted modes\n`ℓ = 0, …, n-1` — i.e. `O_n ≅ ⊕_{ℓ<n} V_ℓ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalSpaceNormalBundle.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.orbitalDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalSpaceNormalBundle.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.orbitalDim","kind":"def","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L206-L206","doc":"The dimension of the orbital space at shell `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalSpaceNormalBundle.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalSpaceNormalBundle.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.mk","kind":"ctor","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L204-L204","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalSpaceNormalBundle.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalSpaceNormalBundle.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark","kind":"class","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L185-L211","doc":"**Borromean-quark orbital-decomposition class** (conditional input for\n`conj:orbital-space-normal-bundle`).\n\nThe conjectural content is the SO(3)-representation-theoretic claim of\nthe sibling `.md` (\"the critical step\"): because the trefoil\n`T_{2,3}` orbits the Borromean proton anchor `𝓑₃` and time-averages to\na topological `S²`, the orbital space at shell `n` decomposes as\n\n  `O_n ≅ V_0 ⊕ V_1 ⊕ ⋯ ⊕ V_{n-1}`,\n\nwhere `V_ℓ` is the SO(3) irreducible of dimension `2ℓ+1`.  The two\ncontent-bearing fields encode exactly that decomposition:\n\n* `orbitalDim` — the dimension functional `n ↦ dim O_n`;\n* `so3_decomposition` — the conjectural input: `dim O_n` equals the sum\n  over the admitted modes `ℓ = 0, …, n-1` of the SO(3)-irrep dimensions\n  `2ℓ+1`.  This is the Borromean-anchor / SO(3) claim, not the\n  conclusion `n²` (which is *derived* below). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.orbital_space_normal_bundle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.orbital_space_normal_bundle","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L161-L166","doc":"The orbital space at shell n has dimension n².\nThis is the declaration referenced by the content manifest\n`prop:orbital-space-normal-bundle`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:orbital-space-normal-bundle","label":"conj:orbital-space-normal-bundle","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.mode_cutoff_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.mode_cutoff_iff","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L156-L159","doc":"Mode cutoff iff: ℓ(ℓ+1) ≤ n(n-1) ↔ ℓ ≤ n-1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.mode_cutoff_conv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.mode_cutoff_conv","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L149-L154","doc":"Converse: ℓ ≤ n-1 ⟹ ℓ(ℓ+1) ≤ n(n-1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.mode_cutoff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.mode_cutoff","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L133-L147","doc":"Mode cutoff: ℓ(ℓ+1) ≤ n(n-1) ⟹ ℓ ≤ n-1.\nProof: contrapositive — if ℓ ≥ n then ℓ(ℓ+1) ≥ n(n+1) > n(n-1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.mode_is_so3_irrep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.mode_is_so3_irrep","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L88-L127","doc":"**Axiom**: For each ℓ, the SO(3) irreducible representation V_ℓ\nhas dimension 2ℓ+1.\n\nIn the QOU context: mode ℓ on the trefoil T_{2,3} ⊂ Σ₄ transforms\nas V_ℓ when the trefoil orbits the Borromean anchor sweeping out S².\n\n## Mathlib status (as of v4.24.0)\n\nAvailable:\n- `Module.finrank` (Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension)\n- SO(3) definable via `Matrix.specialOrthogonalGroup (Fin 3) ℝ`\n\nMissing (not formalized in Mathlib):\n- Peter–Weyl theorem (L²(G) ≅ ⊕ V_π ⊗ V_π*)\n- Classification of SO(3) irreps (highest weight theory)\n- Spherical harmonics Y_ℓ^m as explicit basis for V_ℓ\n- Continuous representations of Lie groups\n\n## Proof route when Mathlib gains these\n\n1. Define `SO3 := Matrix.specialOrthogonalGroup (Fin 3) ℝ`\n2. Apply compact group irrep classification: for each ℓ ∈ ℕ,\n   the unique (up to iso) irreducible real representation V_ℓ\n   has `Module.finrank ℝ V_ℓ = 2 * ℓ + 1`\n3. Peter–Weyl on L²(S²) under the SO(3) action gives\n   L²(S²) ≅ ⊕_{ℓ≥0} V_ℓ with V_ℓ = span{Y_ℓ^m : m = -ℓ..ℓ}\n4. Trefoil averaging: the time-averaged section space of mode ℓ\n   on T_{2,3} projects isomorphically onto V_ℓ ⊂ L²(S²)\n\nSteps 1–3 are standard harmonic analysis; step 4 is the\ngeometry specific to the QOU framework. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.orbital_dim_eq_square","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.orbital_dim_eq_square","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L79-L82","doc":"Dimension of the orbital space at shell n is n² (alternate form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.orbital_space_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.orbital_space_dim","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L69-L77","doc":"The total orbital dimension at shell n is n².\nThis is the purely arithmetic content of the SO(3) decomposition:\nΣ_{ℓ=0}^{n-1} (2ℓ+1) = n². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalDecomposition.total_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalDecomposition.total_dim","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L63-L63","doc":"The total orbital dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalDecomposition.irrep_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalDecomposition.irrep_dim","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The dimension of the ℓ-th irreducible V_ℓ is 2ℓ+1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrbitalDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrbitalDecomposition","kind":"structure","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L48-L63","doc":"The **orbital decomposition** at shell n packages the SO(3)\nrepresentation-theoretic data:\n- n modes (ℓ = 0, 1, …, n−1)\n- Each mode ℓ transforms as the irreducible V_ℓ of dimension 2ℓ+1\n- Total dimension is n²\n\nThis is a purely combinatorial encoding: the geometric content\n(normal-bundle sections, q-Laplacian eigenmodes) is captured by\nthe narrative in the sibling .md file.  The representation-theoretic\nfact — that mode ℓ on the trefoil transforms as V_ℓ under SO(3) —\nis stated as an axiom in `mode_is_so3_irrep`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-space-normal-bundle.lean#L38-L40","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}